# CYS-EPX-mod2-epoxide — alternative mod2 for the epoxide pre-reaction input
#
# When the user uploaded a ligand with the epoxide 3-ring still closed
# (the free-drug SMILES form, e.g. C1OC1R for terminal epoxide or any
# epoxide-bearing inhibitor / probe), this mod2 REPLACES the default
# `data_mod_CYS-EPX-mod2` in CYS-EPX.cif. Encodes the ring-opening
# chemistry that the bond declaration triggers:
#
#   (1) Delete the Cβ-O bond (opens the 3-ring)
#   (2) Add an H atom on the epoxide-O (it becomes -OH on Cα — the H
#       comes from solvent during the opening; nominal H-O distance
#       0.96 Å, but the chem_comp's bond block governs that)
#   (3) Add the O-H bond (links the new hydroxyl H to the O)
#   (4) No carbon retype — both Cα and Cβ stay sp3 (they were sp3 in
#       the strained ring too; ring opening just releases strain)
#   (5) The new SG-Cβ bond is added via the link's bond block (not here)
#
# Selected at runtime when the SMARTS detector matched CYS-EPX-pre
# (epoxide-ring-bearing ligand).
#
# PLACEHOLDER TOKENS substituted at runtime:
#   <CB>  ← Cβ atom-id (the ring C that gets the SG)
#   <CA>  ← Cα atom-id (the ring C that keeps the O)
#   <OE>  ← epoxide-O atom-id
#   <HOE> ← new H to add on the O (becomes the Cα hydroxyl H)

data_mod_CYS-EPX-mod2

# (1) Delete the Cβ-O bond (opens the 3-ring)
# (3) Add the new O-H bond
loop_
_chem_mod_bond.mod_id
_chem_mod_bond.function
_chem_mod_bond.atom_id_1
_chem_mod_bond.atom_id_2
_chem_mod_bond.new_type
_chem_mod_bond.new_value_dist
_chem_mod_bond.new_value_dist_esd
 CYS-EPX-mod2 delete <CB>  <OE>   .     .    .
 CYS-EPX-mod2 add    <OE>  <HOE>  single 0.96 0.01

# (2) Add the new H on O — energy type H (refmac's standard hydroxyl H)
loop_
_chem_mod_atom.mod_id
_chem_mod_atom.function
_chem_mod_atom.atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_symbol
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_energy
_chem_mod_atom.new_partial_charge
 CYS-EPX-mod2 add    <HOE> <HOE> H H .
